@startuml
' Source of truth for: assets/diagrams/learning/data-plane/ngfw/ipsec-control-data-split.svg
' Re-render with: plantuml -tsvg ipsec-control-data-split.puml
title IPsec: Negotiate Once (control), Encrypt Always (data)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleRoundCorner 8
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

package "CONTROL PLANE — occasional negotiation" {
  rectangle "VICI clients (automation)\ncreate_ipsec.py (load_conn / PSK / initiate)\nswanctl_bridge.py (list / rekey / terminate)\nVPP CLI -> popen python3 (ngfw_swanctl ...)" as CLIENTS #fff7ed
  rectangle "StrongSwan charon\nthe IKE daemon\nIKEv2: authenticate peer, agree ciphers,\nderive ESP keys -> SAs" as CHARON #ffedd5
  rectangle "Remote VPN peer" as PEER #f1f5f9
}

package "DATA PLANE — per-packet encryption" {
  rectangle "kernel-vpp plugin (the bridge)\nreplaces StrongSwan's Linux-kernel backend\ninstalls each SA into VPP, auto-binds to\nthe tunnel iface, refreshes on rekey" as BRIDGE #fff1f2
  rectangle "VPP data plane\nesp-encrypt / esp-decrypt\nSA table (keys + SPIs) indexed by out_sa_index\nbound to tunnel interface" as VPP #f0fdfa
}

CLIENTS -> CHARON : VICI socket\n/var/run/charon.vici
CHARON <-> PEER : IKE (UDP 500/4500)
CHARON --> BRIDGE
BRIDGE --> VPP : install SA
VPP -> PEER : encrypted ESP packets
@enduml
